    {
      "page_title": "Drop: Destructors",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Underscore Trap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let _ = lock.lock();      // dropped NOW",
            "let _guard = lock.lock(); // held to scope end"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bare `_` is not a binding — it drops immediately",
            "`_guard` still binds and still lives to end of scope",
            "This is the classic silent critical-section bug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Temporaries Die At The `;`",
          "text": "They drop at the end of the enclosing statement, not the block. Hence surprise early releases in `match` scrutinees and method chains."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Suppressing And Failing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ManuallyDrop<T>` and `mem::forget` suppress the destructor",
            "Leaking is safe in Rust; unsoundness is not",
            "Panics run drops while unwinding — no leaks on failure paths",
            "A panic inside `drop` while unwinding aborts the process"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Resources That Use It"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "What drop does"
